Falsifies
`driver_process_contract::non_volatile_memory_express::proofs::the_spawn_handoff_round_trips`.

The defect: `Handoff::pack` shifts `blocks_per_transfer` by 17 where `unpack` reads from bit 16. The
data plane then addresses twice the LBA it was told, and nothing between the two halves notices.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert_eq!(Handoff::unpack(h.pack()), Some(h))`.

diff --git a/crates/driver_process_contract/src/non_volatile_memory_express.rs b/crates/driver_process_contract/src/non_volatile_memory_express.rs
--- a/crates/driver_process_contract/src/non_volatile_memory_express.rs
+++ b/crates/driver_process_contract/src/non_volatile_memory_express.rs
@@ -139,7 +139,7 @@
     pub fn pack(&self) -> [u64; 3] {
         [
             (self.dstrd as u64) << 32
-                | (self.blocks_per_transfer as u64) << 16
+                | (self.blocks_per_transfer as u64) << 17
                 | self.entries as u64,
             self.data_plane_physical_address,
             self.size_bytes,
